# Starting Point Consulting — environment variables.
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in. Never commit `.env`.
#
# CLAUDE.md, "Hosting and ownership model": the build lives on Hadley's
# accounts now and transfers to accounts Darlene owns at completion. Nothing
# account-specific is hardcoded in app logic — it all comes from here, so the
# transfer is a matter of swapping these values.

# --- Supabase (added in Phase 5; the schema and RLS policies must be
#     approved in plain English before any of this is used) ---

# Safe to expose to the browser. Reads only what RLS allows anonymously.
PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# SERVER ONLY. Never prefix with PUBLIC_, never import into client code.
#
# Used to mint a 60-second token whose role claim is sp_writer — the Postgres
# role created by supabase/migrations/0001_initial_schema.sql, which holds
# INSERT on two tables and cannot read a single row. This is the "restricted
# insert-only path, not a role that can also read" that CLAUDE.md requires.
#
# Supabase dashboard -> Project Settings -> API -> JWT Settings -> JWT Secret.
SUPABASE_JWT_SECRET=

# NOT USED, and deliberately so. The service-role key carries Postgres
# BYPASSRLS: it ignores every policy in the migration, so a leak would expose
# every intake submission and CSA acceptance. The public site never uses it.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
